#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197987 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bfe2e3e-9d7b-5c53-8de8-2717237d3e9c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Uniform Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/id #uuid "88848c23-66fe-5937-958c-28d73b593d99" :question/math-academy-id "e-12487" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 3, \\:\\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 2 \\big\\}$. Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$, we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_x$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n$R_x = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_x}{M}}$,\nwhere $I_x$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n- The radius of gyration $R_y$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n$R_y = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_y}{M}}$,\nwhere $I_y$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n- The radius of gyration $R_0$ about the origin is given by\n$R_0 = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_0}{M}}$,\nwhere $I_0$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\nI_y = \\iint\\limits_D x^2\\lambda(x,y) \\:\\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = 3\\cdot 1 = 3\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = \\dfrac{M}{\\mathcal{A}} = \\dfrac{M}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI_{y} &= ∬_(D)x^{2}λ(x, y)dA \\\\\n&= \\frac{M}{3}∫_{1}^{2}∫_{0}^{3}x^{2}dxdy \\\\\n&= \\frac{M}{3}∫_{1}^{2}[\\frac{1}{3}x^{3}]_{0}^{3}dy \\\\\n&= \\frac{M}{3}∫_{1}^{2}9dy \\\\\n&= 3M∫_{1}^{2}dy \\\\\n&= 3M[y]_{1}^{2} \\\\\n&= 3M(2 - 1) \\\\\n&= 3M\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nR_y^2 =\\dfrac{3M}{M} = 3\\quad \\Rightarrow\\quad R_y = \\sqrt{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197989 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "068d9714-bd1e-5036-a0c7-9be288831f52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Radii of Gyration Using Polar Coordinates"}] :question/id #uuid "fa3e8249-cb9f-50f6-a56f-6f311d101de6" :question/math-academy-id "e-12495" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies one-half of the circle $x^2+y^2\\leq 1$ for $y\\geq 0$. Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda(x,y)=\\dfrac{3}{2}My$. Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$, we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_x$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n$R_x = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_x}{M}}$,\nwhere $I_x$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n- The radius of gyration $R_y$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n$R_y = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_y}{M}}$,\nwhere $I_y$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n- The radius of gyration $R_0$ about the origin is given by\n$R_0 = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_0}{M}}$,\nwhere $I_0$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{(r,\\theta) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq r \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\pi \\right\\}\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\nI_0 = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda(r,\\theta) r^3 \\:\\textrm{d}r\\:\\textrm{d}\\theta\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(r,\\theta)$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is\n\n$$\n\\lambda(r,\\theta)=\\dfrac{3}{2}Mr\\sin\\theta\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI_{0} &= ∬_(D)λ(r, θ)r^{3}drdθ \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{2}M∫_{0}^{π}∫_{0}^{1}r^{4}\\sin θdrdθ \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{2}M(∫_{0}^{1}r^{4}dr)(∫_{0}^{π}\\sin θdθ) \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{2}M \\cdot \\frac{1}{5}r^{5} \\mid _{0}^{1} \\cdot (-\\cos θ) \\mid _{0}^{π} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{2}M \\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\cdot 2 \\\\\n&= \\frac{3M}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nR_{0} &= \\sqrt{\\frac{I_{0}}{M}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{3M}{5} \\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197991 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Non-Uniform, Non-Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/id #uuid "5245b67a-8beb-512d-b3c8-2d38db797703" :question/math-academy-id "e-12507" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the lines $y = x$, $x = 1$, and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda(x,y) = 3Mx$. Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$, we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_x$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n$R_x = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_x}{M}}$,\nwhere $I_x$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n- The radius of gyration $R_y$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n$R_y = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_y}{M}}$,\nwhere $I_y$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n- The radius of gyration $R_0$ about the origin is given by\n$R_0 = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_0}{M}}$,\nwhere $I_0$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\nI_0 = \\iint\\limits_D (x^2 + y^2) \\lambda(x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq x \\right\\}\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI_{0} &= ∬_(D)(x^{2} + y^{2})λ(x, y)dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{x}(x^{2} + y^{2}) \\cdot 3Mxdydx \\\\\n&= 3M∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{x}x^{3} + xy^{2}dydx \\\\\n&= 3M∫_{0}^{1}[x^{3}y + \\frac{1}{3}xy^{3}]_{y = 0}^{y = x}dx \\\\\n&= 3M∫_{0}^{1}x^{4} + \\frac{1}{3}x^{4}dx \\\\\n&= 3M∫_{0}^{1}\\frac{4}{3}x^{4}dx \\\\\n&= 3M[\\frac{4}{15}x^{5}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= 3M \\cdot \\frac{4}{15} \\\\\n&= \\frac{4M}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nR_{0} &= \\sqrt{\\frac{I_{0}}{M}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{4M}{5} \\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{5}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bfe2e3e-9d7b-5c53-8de8-2717237d3e9c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Uniform Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b02d9443-7864-5741-b395-c24abbd2b736" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{19}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194370} {:answer/id #uuid "d11dee5f-f185-5b9b-85b7-29b8b08efaa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194371} {:answer/id #uuid "d5d1d883-ab40-5185-ad71-55d14ca345ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194372} {:answer/id #uuid "3ff3388e-32ae-523f-9c3f-7f1f093b9f28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194373} {:answer/id #uuid "5dbd58b5-99a0-5f3a-a047-c107325e40e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d11dee5f-f185-5b9b-85b7-29b8b08efaa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194371} :answer-field/id #uuid "abd0743b-879f-59db-972f-80ec21ea6912" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194369}] :question/id #uuid "5e1eb104-83e6-5dc7-913b-3996107f92c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-163011" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n\n$D = {(x, y): 0 \\le x \\le 2, 1 \\le y \\le 3}$. Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198591 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Non-Uniform, Non-Rectangular Laminar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cacc079-86bb-5220-a40f-8de5c9b8e07e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194448} {:answer/id #uuid "d79108fb-d801-52ba-9648-47fa212c3fe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194449} {:answer/id #uuid "41c4018b-c4f8-57ea-bd03-fc8883e007ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194450} {:answer/id #uuid "4d75ca10-6598-54e6-af76-86b267fba7bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194451} {:answer/id #uuid "6f9ef8a1-d1a7-5488-b4b2-2cc2dda43c4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41c4018b-c4f8-57ea-bd03-fc8883e007ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194450} :answer-field/id #uuid "367d03c1-12cd-5b35-bf55-9c5e6d150f37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194447}]